This time you ain't
shooting no liquor bottles.

267
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:57,060
This time is live, one-on-one combat.

268
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,760
You mean you didn't know?!

269
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:03,860
Can I drop out now?

270
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:07,708
You dragged me into this with
you and now it's too damn late!

271
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:25,817
You're very lucky, mister.

272
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:27,312
It's only your shoulder.

273
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:30,557
You're good at changing trajectories.

274
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:33,137
You don't like seeing
people kill each other, huh?

275
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:35,257
Remember, you're the one
who dragged me into this.

276
00:15:35,340 --> 00:15:36,516
No need to thank me.

277
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:40,740
We will now commence the
first quarterfinal match.

278
00:15:44,340 --> 00:15:46,740
It's you and me, spineless coward.

279
00:15:46,940 --> 00:15:47,937
Please go easy on me.

280
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:49,057
I'm really scared.

281
00:15:49,140 --> 00:15:50,380
Ready, go!

282
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:08,497
Not bad.

283
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:09,420
Nice...shot.

284
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:12,840
He was facing backwards
the whole time. Snake.

285
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,537
This is unusual.

286
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:38,757
So far we haven't had a single
fatality in this year's contest. Hell.

287
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:40,737
He's actually the real thing.

288
00:16:40,820 --> 00:16:42,760
He's Vash the Stampede.

289
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:49,480
now you're cool enough
to join our club mr.

290
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:52,617
wolfwood just told me that he's going
to step out of the competition so i

291
00:16:52,700 --> 00:16:57,112
guess that means now you've won this
contest for sure isn't that wonderful?

292
00:16:57,980 --> 00:17:01,677
i'm nicholas d wolfwood i'm
withdrawing from the final round

293
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:07,257
really but you were doing so
well for yourself may i ask why?

294
00:17:07,340 --> 00:17:11,137
oh it's too much of a bother that's all
just give the prize to the other guy!

295
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:13,537
all right i can't do that!

296
00:17:13,620 --> 00:17:15,737
what? look? huh?

297
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:20,920
well now that's how it is

298
00:17:21,320 --> 00:17:23,420
Nicholas, you really are very good.

299
00:17:23,900 --> 00:17:28,560
Would you consider eliminating Vash the
Stampede with your superb gunmanship?

300
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:33,260
If you do as I ask, I will guarantee
you the safety of that family.

301
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:38,520
And I'd even be willing to raise the
prize to 30 billion double dollars.

302
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:41,100
You mean 50-50?

303
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:44,231
I like a man with a head on his shoulders.

304
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:46,811
Gentlemen, the final round will now begin!

305
00:18:00,180 --> 00:18:01,840
Ah! But why?

306
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:03,830
No, Vash!

307
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:10,136
Didn't you go over there to withdraw?

308
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:11,977
Here's the big money question.

309
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:16,001
Tell me, what do you see in the
window of that building over there?

310
00:18:18,620 --> 00:18:20,540
And that just about sums it up.

311
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:22,570
Ready, go!

312
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:28,190
Run, Ash!

313
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:31,297
It's for the good of the family.

314
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:33,086
Just resign yourself and die.

315
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:36,900
Come on, get serious.

316
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:40,297
I'm saying that we all have
to make a few sacrifices.

317
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:41,968
Can I make a different one?

318
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:45,520
Now you've done it.

319
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:49,517
Well, this is what you got me
so plastered for yesterday.

320
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:52,482
Do you really think I'd
try something that cheap?

321
00:18:53,020 --> 00:18:53,880
Yeah, I do!

322
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:56,217
After you went and signed
me up without asking...

323
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:58,320
You did the same to me!

324
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:26,420
Now the sixty billion double dollars is
all mine how fortunate now finish them off

325
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:30,100
Ahh!

326
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:44,240
What?

327
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:03,930
What?

328
00:20:04,013 --> 00:20:05,260
Why don't you kill them?

329
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:10,490
Help!

330
00:20:10,573 --> 00:20:11,403
Throw me my luggage!

331
00:20:12,580 --> 00:20:13,410
Huh?

332
00:20:13,493 --> 00:20:14,340
But it's too big!

333
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:16,480
Come on, we can do it!

334
00:20:17,140 --> 00:20:18,180
Step aside!

335
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:19,811
I'm gonna give it a push!

336
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:28,860
Hey, don't kill them!

337
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:34,769
Hey, whatever happens,
thou shalt not kill!

338
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:57,880
I won't let any more children suffer,

339
00:20:58,280 --> 00:20:59,960
never again!

340
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:11,354
Wow, this is horrible.

341
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:13,038
I don't understand.

342
00:21:13,460 --> 00:21:15,717
Why did you have to go and
injure so many of these people?

343
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:18,212
What kind of a churchman are you, anyway?

344
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:19,757
Hey, it's no big deal.

345
00:21:19,840 --> 00:21:21,605
Nobody's dead, I kept my word.

346
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:22,790
Now then.

347
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:26,147
Mister, may the Lord
have mercy on your soul.

348
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:29,657
Or do you intend to pay me
the prize money after all?

349
00:21:29,740 --> 00:21:32,337
All right, then. I'll pay it. I'll pay it.

350
00:21:32,420 --> 00:21:33,680
Much obliged.

351
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:47,137
He sure has become awfully popular
all of a sudden, don't you think?

352
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:51,480
I knew he was no ordinary priest,
but I had no idea how unusual he was.

353
00:21:54,600 --> 00:21:56,200
I can't hit you now!

354
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:02,320
There you are.

355
00:22:03,220 --> 00:22:04,500
Thank you so much.

356
00:22:04,780 --> 00:22:06,545
Ah, heck, think nothing of it.

357
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:10,238
What's wrong, Neil?

358
00:22:14,060 --> 00:22:14,890
Dad!

359
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:16,630
Dear!

360
00:22:17,220 --> 00:22:18,500
Guess my job is done.

361
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:20,172
Yep, sure looks like it.

362
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:24,140
For love and peace. Huh?

363
00:22:26,040 --> 00:22:27,120
Get off!

364
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:29,310
No, Captain!

365
00:22:29,393 --> 00:22:31,100
Anything but that! No!

366
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:32,710
No!

367
00:24:06,400 --> 00:24:08,420
A choice between two things.

368
00:24:08,860 --> 00:24:14,740
A forked road, a cross road, where men
given life must take in order to stay alive.

369
00:24:15,760 --> 00:24:18,740
Whichever end they live
on, they lose something.

370
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:23,047
Whichever end they live on, they
are unable to find happiness.

371
00:24:23,540 --> 00:24:26,960
But, are there really only
two paths to a forked road?

372
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:30,671
No, there are infinite paths we must take.

373
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:32,960
There is more than one path.

374
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:35,751
There is more than one path to the future.
